W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c2: 8-stratum × 5-knob per-knob ablation audit
===================================================================

Date: 2026-05-24
Parent commit:  cc081ff5 docs(W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1): honest-stop on screen/very_high k2 floor
This commit:    <added by SHIPPED commit>

Hypothesis
----------
The W44-PHASE4-S2-refit lookup (commit 2991bb27) was rebaked from the
post-W44-RECON-DEEP corpus. W44-228c1 SHIP-cell validation caught a
catastrophe on terminal e8 d=4 (Mode A baseline 42322 B/SSIM2 86.91 →
Mode B opt-in 28185 B/SSIM2 81.98, ΔSSIM2 -4.93). W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1
HONEST-STOPPED after a single-knob k2 sweep on terminal e8 d=4 produced
byte-identical output at every k2; isolated k1=0 with other knobs at
defaults reproduced the catastrophe.

c2 hypothesis: other strata in the S2-refit lookup may carry similar
hidden cliffs. Need to audit all 8 strata × 5 knobs (= 40 ablation
measurements) to surface and repair them all in one pass.

Method
------
Single-process-per-encode harness (`examples/w44_phase4_s2_refit_c2_ablate.rs`):
takes explicit (k1, k2, k3, k4, k5) via CLI flags, encodes one cell,
emits one TSV row. Works around runtime::install OnceLock single-shot.

For each of 8 strata, the orchestration script
(`scripts/run_w44_phase4_s2_refit_c2_audit.sh`) runs 7 encodes:
- baseline_defaults: all knobs at production defaults (= byte-identical
  to no-opt-in path; serves as the "what would users see by default" anchor)
- full_s2refit: the stratum-specific (k1..k5) tuple from src/tuning.rs
- 5 ablations: k_i_default = full_s2refit but with knob k_i reset to
  default. If reset closes the cliff, k_i is the lever.

= 56 encodes. Plus 13 follow-up encodes on screen/very_high + screen/high
(multi-knob neighbourhood probes + (k1, k2) bisection on screen/very_high
+ k1 floor bisection on screen/high) to identify the floor floors.

Cell selection (one per stratum):
- screen/very_high: terminal.png e8 d=4 (the W44-105 SHIP cell)
- screen/high:      graph.png e8 d=3
- screen/mid:       graph.png e8 d=1.5
- screen/low:       graph.png e8 d=0.7
- photo/very_high:  CID22 1531677.png e8 d=5
- photo/high:       CID22 1189261.png e8 d=3
- photo/mid:        CID22 1025469.png e8 d=1.5
- photo/low:        CID22 1418519.png e8 d=0.7

Metrics: bytes, butteraugli (Rust crate, linear-RGB inputs), SSIMULACRA2
(fast_ssim2). Multi-decoder roundtrip via jxl-oxide for decode (planar
linear). 2 timing trials per encode (best wall reported; bytes/metrics
deterministic).

Per-stratum verdict
-------------------
6 CLEAN — no cliff:
  - photo/very_high, photo/high, photo/mid, photo/low: ALL 7 rows
    byte-identical (Tier-2 dispatch doesn't fire on these cells at
    their distances).
  - screen/low: ALL 7 rows byte-identical (graph d=0.7 below dispatch).
  - screen/mid: full_s2refit gives +0.47 SSIM2 WIN; no cliff direction
    on any knob.

2 REPAIRABLE — multi-knob structural cliff:
  - screen/very_high (terminal e8 d=4 SHIP cell): full_s2refit ΔSSIM2
    -4.93; single-k1-default ablation actually makes it WORSE (-10.18);
    single-k2/k3/k4/k5 default ablations all byte-identical to
    full_s2refit (no effect). Two-knob (k1=0.5, k2=1.0) restore →
    SSIM2 +0.13 vs baseline. The cliff has TWO joint drivers (k1=0
    AND k2=0).
  - screen/high (graph e8 d=3): full_s2refit ΔSSIM2 -5.07; single-k1
    partially recovers to -1.94 (over ±0.5 budget); two-knob
    (k1=0.5, k2=1.0) restore → SSIM2 -0.10 vs baseline.

0 STRUCTURALLY BROKEN — well below the 4-stratum honest-stop trigger.

(k1, k2) bisection on screen/very_high (other knobs at S2-refit)
-----------------------------------------------------------------

| k1   | k2    | bytes   | SSIM2  | ΔSSIM2 vs baseline 86.91 |
|------|-------|---------|--------|--------------------------|
| 0.25 | 0.333 | 28185   | 81.98  | -4.93 (cliff)            |
| 0.25 | 0.5   | 28185   | 81.98  | -4.93 (cliff)            |
| 0.25 | 1.0   | 28185   | 81.98  | -4.93 (cliff)            |
| 0.333| 0.333 | 33709   | 82.71  | -4.20                    |
| 0.333| 0.5   | 36001   | 86.22  | -0.69                    |
| 0.333| 1.0   | 43755   | 87.01  | +0.10                    |
| 0.5  | 0.333 | 33903   | 82.72  | -4.19                    |
| 0.5  | 0.5   | 36232   | 86.23  | -0.68                    |
| 0.5  | 1.0   | 43989   | 87.04  | +0.13 ✓                  |

Reading: k1 ≤ 0.25 cliffs at ANY k2 (p1 saturates at ridge max ~145).
k1 ≥ 0.333 + k2 ≥ 1.0 satisfies ±0.5 SSIM2. Smallest joint floor that
clears the budget on the SHIP cell is (k1=0.5, k2=1.0) = defaults.

c2 fix
------
Updated jxl-encoder/src/tuning.rs::default_for_stratum:
- ScreenVeryHigh: (0.0, 0.0, 0.5, 2.167, -0.333) → (0.5, 1.0, 0.5, 2.167, -0.333)
- ScreenHigh:     (0.0, 0.333, 0.5, 2.167, -0.667) → (0.5, 1.0, 0.5, 2.167, -0.667)
- All 6 other strata unchanged (CLEAN).

k3/k4/k5 retained at S2-refit values: they're byte-identical no-ops on
the SHIP cells per the ablation table, but may still affect other cells
in those strata per the original sweep data.

Test `w44_phase4_s2_refit_strata_aggressiveness_membership` updated:
- Removes ScreenVeryHigh from the k2==0 set (now k2==1.0)
- Removes ScreenHigh from the k2==0.333 set (now k2==1.0)
- Adds a new assertion block enforcing (k1==0.5, k2==1.0) on both
  ScreenVeryHigh + ScreenHigh as binding W44-105 SHIP-cell protection
  invariants.

