What this audit found that c1 missed
------------------------------------
c1 ran ONLY k2 ∈ {0..1.5} sweeps on terminal e8 d=4 in Mode B (with
other knobs at S2-refit values) and saw byte-identical output at every
k2. c1 then ran ONE isolated test (k1=0 + all other knobs at defaults)
that reproduced the catastrophe. From these two measurements c1
concluded "k1 IS the lever; k2 is NOT."

c1's reading was correct that k1 is NECESSARY but incomplete — the c2
ablation showed k1 alone is NOT SUFFICIENT. From the FULL S2-refit
tuple, resetting k1 alone (single-default ablation) makes screen/very_high
WORSE (-10.18 ΔSSIM2). Resetting k2 alone has zero effect. Only resetting
BOTH k1 AND k2 restores within ±0.5.

The mechanism: k1=0 → p1 ridge-max → admit-gate disruption; k2=0 → p3
zeroed → W44-105 lift removed. Both can independently destabilize the
SHIP-cell encoder path; restoring just one leaves the other active.

The c2 audit also surfaced a SECOND cliff on screen/high (graph e8 d=3),
which c1 didn't check at all. Same mechanism: k1=0 + k2=0.333 jointly
cliffs SSIM2 by 5.07. Same fix: (k1=0.5, k2=1.0) restore.

DO NOT (future agents)
----------------------
- DO NOT lower k1 below 0.5 OR k2 below 1.0 on screen/very_high or
  screen/high without re-running the c2 (k1, k2) bisection.
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte movement here (per W44-66
  user correction).
- DO NOT add a single-knob k1 floor below 0.5 (c2 audit proved
  insufficient).
- DO NOT respawn c2/c3 chunks trying single-knob fixes on these strata.
- DO NOT attempt to ship the raw S2-refit screen/very_high or
  screen/high values without a corresponding zenanalyze sub-discriminator
  that routes terminal/graph-class SHIP cells around the lookup.

Follow-on candidates (NOT this chunk)
-------------------------------------
1. Per-image zenanalyze sub-discriminator (W44-91/96 pattern) that
   admits raw S2-refit only when the image is NOT in the W44-105 SHIP
   cluster — would unlock the predicted +37.4% / +13.7% coverage gain
   on other screen/very_high + screen/high cells.
2. Re-derive S2-refit with a Pareto criterion that scores against bytes
   AND SSIM2 (not bytes alone), AND includes the W44-105 SHIP cells in
   the corpus.
3. Future sweep selector multi-knob neighborhood validation: a single-
   marginal-PDP selector cannot detect joint cliffs in (k1, k2); add
   a pre-commit SHIP-cell probe to the per-stratum optima derivation.
